(version 1)

# CEC EPS 8-pin module — custom design rules.
# KiCad auto-loads <board>.kicad_dru from the project dir. These back the netclasses
# in eps8pin-module.kicad_pro: a netclass `track_width` is only the *routing default*,
# so DRC will NOT flag an under-width power trace on its own. The constraints below
# make DRC actually catch the cases that matter, and leave the high-current pours and
# the shunt-shared Kelvin taps alone (a per-track floor would false-flag them).

# +5VSB / +3V3 / VBUS (Power netclass): 0.5mm track floor (~2.4A at 2oz). The +5VSB
# trunk from the RJ-45 VCC pin + the USB-VBUS OR feeds the LDO and CAN; 0.5mm is the
# minimum for that branch current.
(rule "Power min width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'Power'"))

# NO per-track width floor on the +12V rails (Power12V = /SENSEC*). Their ~30A/cable
# ampacity comes from the F.Cu + B.Cu 2oz POURS (split at each shunt, verified by pour
# copper area per IPC-2152), NOT from individual track width. The four-wire Kelvin
# sense taps (INA238 + INA181) live ON these same SENSEC nets and are drawn as ~0.25mm
# stubs off the shunt's inner edges, so a Power12V track-width floor would wrongly flag
# them. Draw the Kelvin tap stub by hand with the 0.25mm preset; size the rail copper
# from the pour area in the GUI.

# USB 2.0 Full-Speed pair (USB netclass): /USB_D_P / /USB_D_N are renamed to the _P/_N
# convention so KiCad auto-recognizes the differential pair. Keep D+/D- coupled; FS
# (ESP32-C6 native USB-Serial-JTAG) is impedance-tolerant, but flag long uncoupled runs.
(rule "USB diff pair gap"
	(constraint diff_pair_gap (min 0.1mm) (max 0.2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'USB' && B.NetClass == 'USB'"))

# CAN (CAN netclass): CAN_H / CAN_L keep the standard (semantically asymmetric) names,
# so they are NOT an auto-recognized P/N pair -- route them as a tightly-coupled pair by
# hand to the RJ-45. No impedance rule (short stub, <=1Mbps); the only termination is the
# Hub's split 120R, never on the module.
